<title>UK: BOE BUYS 147 MLN STG BILLS, 1.050 BLN SHORTAGE.</title>
<headline>BOE BUYS 147 MLN STG BILLS, 1.050 BLN SHORTAGE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England bought 147 million stg of bills in a combination of outright purchases and repo to help offset today's estimated money market shortage of 1.050 billion stg.</p>
<p>The Bank's repo rate was unchanged at 7.0 percent.</p>
<p>Outright purchases totalled 7.0 million stg and repo 140 million.</p>
</text>
